{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact pushed head 5378957a52b4e3b158fdcb00060f1806e2bb3466, one commit on base c3169d83 (current main and origin/main), two files only, Rests-On the implementation request 4d01ad58, clean detached checkout matching origin. Independently reproduced in a scratch bare-origin plus actions/checkout-style feature-branch runner clone, running the resolve and run scripts extracted verbatim from the workflow YAML at the head: 25 of 25 checks pass. Bare main does not resolve in the old direct pass-through (rev-parse has no DWIM to refs/remotes/origin/main), confirming the defect; the new resolver resolves default base=main, HEAD, and exact 40-hex SHAs to truthful immutable commits; revision expressions (main~1, HEAD^, a..b, main:path), option-shaped input, dot-prefixed and spaced names are all rejected before fetch, writing nothing to GITHUB_ENV; an unknown SHA fails without fetching; and with origin advanced and the remote URL broken, the fetch failure exits nonzero writing nothing while local refs/remotes/origin/main holds a stale value. Stripping the explicit || return guards makes the same scenario exit 0 and emit the stale SHA — errexit is cleared inside command substitution in both bash 3.2 and 5.2 — proving each guard load-bearing. Bare return after || return propagates the failing status, and rev-parse --verify with ^{commit} peel emits only a single lowercase 40-hex line, so no GITHUB_ENV line injection exists; check-ref-format rejects control characters including newline. Scheduled behavior verified with a PATH-stubbed go: schedule yields exactly --base HEAD^ --candidate HEAD --tier smoke, dispatch passes the resolved SHAs through, and a missing resolve-step env fails under set -u instead of comparing silently. permissions contents:read, the comparison command, and the checkout credential posture are unchanged: performance.yml at approved credential head 065d16fd is byte-identical to base and the diff does not touch the checkout step. Gates at the exact head: focused static test passes and fails against the c3169d83 workflow (mutation-confirmed), YAML parses, git diff --check clean, go vet ./... clean, full go test ./... exit 0, make build OK. A second fresh adversarial review pass concurred with approval. Architecture: only the CI performance-evidence workflow and the public repository surface static test are touched; none of the seven layers in docs/reference/architecture.md carries a contract over these files, so every layer contract is preserved and no architecture page update is required. Security: the change strictly tightens the untrusted workflow_dispatch input boundary — inputs are validated (anchored hex regex, check-ref-format) and always used behind refs/heads/ or refs/remotes/origin/ prefixes with --end-of-options, so no argv option or refspec injection path exists; the non-forced fetch refspec fails closed on non-fast-forward moves; persist-credentials false keeps the in-step fetch unauthenticated and it fails closed if unavailable; every validation and fetch failure aborts the step before GITHUB_ENV is written; gitseq-perf independently re-verifies both refs as defense in depth. No unresolved security defect. Simplification: nothing removable without weakening the conditions; the \u003e/dev/null on check-ref-format is dead output redirection and the || return on the SHA-path rev-parse is technically redundant before its bare return, but both are harmless, defensively clear, and pinned by the static test — not worth churn. Two non-blocking follow-up observations for a future head, not conditions of this approval: the static test does not pin the GITHUB_EVENT_NAME guard around the scheduled fallback (making the assignments unconditional passes the test while discarding resolved dispatch refs) and does not pin set -euo pipefail; gitseq-perf re-verification bounds both. Do not merge, per the request; the verdict awaits the requester's ratification.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2